@startuml
!include style.puml
title Graceful shutdown

participant "SIGTERM\n/ SIGINT" as sig
participant "Broker" as b $broker
participant "Worker k" as w $worker
participant "App" as app $usercode
participant "Home Assistant" as ha $ha

sig -> b : signal (needs ext-pcntl)
b -> b : stop probing and restarting workers

b -> w : **Shutdown** { reason, grace }
w -> app : dispose()
app --> w
w -> w : fail all pending\nservice-call futures
note right of w
  Anything still awaiting a result would
  otherwise hang a fiber through shutdown.
end note

w --> b : **returns** from the entrypoint callable
note right of w
  Returning, never exit(). The result channel is
  written only after the callable returns, so
  exiting turns a clean stop into a
  ContextException in the broker.
end note

b -> w : join() until grace + 1 s
alt returned in time
    w --> b : summary string
else grace expired
    b -> w !! : context->close()  <<kill>>
end

b -> ha : close WebSocket
@enduml
